{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=timer-dwork-softirq-lock; Search only snapshots/s03 and no other snapshot. Hunt the timer-softirq analogue of the seed's missing-BH-disable invariant: lock objects acquired inside timer-softirq-context callback bodies (timer_list function callbacks, hrtimer handlers, delayed_work timer-expiry callbacks) that are also taken with plain spin_lock() rather than spin_lock_bh() or local_bh_disable() from process-context paths such as workqueue workers, ioctls, open/close, configuration and firmware requests, so a timer softirq firing on the same CPU spins on a lock the preempted holder can never release. For every candidate record the lock name, the timer-callback-side and process-side call chains with file:line, and the missing bottom-half-disable guarantee; the staging ks7010 seed is a demonstration only and must never be reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s03 with candidates plus exact source evidence, or a negative result backed by concrete source evidence."}
