{"event":"intent","sources":["f001"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=tasklet-napi-softirq-lock; Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot. Hunt the tasklet/NAPI-softirq analogue of the seed's missing-BH-disable invariant: lock objects shared between process-context code (workqueue workers, ioctls, open/close, configuration and firmware request handlers) and code that executes in TASKLET or NET softirq context — tasklet_schedule/tasklet_hi_schedule callback bodies, NAPI poll functions reached via napi_schedule, or other NET_RX/NET_TX softirq callbacks — where the process-context side takes the lock with plain spin_lock() instead of spin_lock_bh()/local_bh_disable(), so a softirq on the same CPU spins forever against a holder that can never resume (soft-lockup, RCU stall, denial of service). Exclude xmit-callback and timer-callback paths already covered by the xmit-softirq-lock and timer-dwork-softirq-lock branches. For every candidate record the lock name, the softirq-side and process-side call chains with file:line, and the missing bottom-half-disable guarantee; the staging ks7010 seed is a demonstration only and must never be reported. Save a structured artifact for snapshots/s01 with candidates plus exact source evidence, or a negative result backed by concrete source evidence."}
